  "kind": "one-step",
  "claim": "A bird that crosses an edge re-enters from the opposite edge; one that stays inside is untouched.",
  "derivation": [
    "World 20 × 20 with every rule off, so velocities are unchanged (E8, E9).",
    "A at (19.99, 5) moving (3, 0) reaches x = 19.99 + 0.05 = 20.04, which wraps to 0.04 (E10).",
    "C at (7, 0.01) moving (0, −2) reaches y = 0.01 − 0.033333 = −0.023333, which wraps to 19.976667.",
    "B at (5, 15) moving (0, −1) stays inside: y = 15 − 1/60 = 14.983333."
  ],
